---
// Hero — headline + three by-the-numbers stat callouts.
---
<section class="hero container" id="top">
  <div class="hero__grid">
    <div>
      <div class="eyebrow">Statewide California Operations</div>
      <h1 class="hero__headline">
        Taking back homes <br />
        for <span class="accent">people,</span> <br />
        not corporations.
      </h1>
      <p class="hero__deck">
        Robin Hood Homes, LLC purchases post-foreclosure properties across California
        through the SB 1079 program — turning what was lost into permanently affordable
        housing. Profits flow back to our home base in Sonoma County to fund community
        programs.
      </p>
      <div class="hero__cta">
        <a href="#how" class="btn btn--primary">
          How it works <span class="arrow">→</span>
        </a>
        <a href="#money" class="btn btn--outline">
          Follow the money
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <aside class="hero__side">
      <div class="hero__rule">By the Numbers</div>

      <div class="hero__stat">
        <div class="num tabular">
          30<small>yrs</small>
        </div>
        <p>Affordable-housing deed restriction recorded on every property we acquire.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="hero__stat">
        <div class="num tabular">
          45<small>days</small>
        </div>
        <p>Post-foreclosure purchase window — 15 days to file, 30 to fund.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="hero__stat">
        <div class="num tabular"><span class="currency">$</span>125<small>K</small></div>
        <p>Granted to Sonoma County nonprofits so far in 2026 &mdash; $50K in Q1, $75K in Q2.</p>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </div>
</section>
